# pnpm's default (isolated) linker, deliberately -- NOT maximal-electron's
# `node-linker=hoisted`.
#
# maximal-electron sets hoisted because Electron Forge packages native
# prebuilds (node-pty, node-llama-cpp) for the final app and does not follow
# pnpm's symlinked store. node-linker is a workspace-root setting, so its
# package-level .npmrc has no effect here and the choice has to be made once,
# for everyone.
#
# Hoisted loses: it empties every package-local node_modules (everything lands
# at the root), and maximal-core's build refuses to bundle without one --
# `bun build` writes module paths relative to the resolved build root, so a
# bundle built without package-local deps is not byte-comparable.
#
# Isolated wins here because this workspace runs tsc, bun test and vitest, none
# of which need a flat tree. The cost is that `electron-forge package/make` is
# not expected to work from this workspace. See README, "Divergence to watch".

# Electron Forge refuses to run under pnpm unless node-linker=hoisted OR a
# hoist pattern is defined. Hoisting outright breaks maximal-core's build
# (it needs a package-local node_modules), so define a pattern instead:
# it satisfies Forge's check while the isolated linker keeps package-local
# trees intact.
public-hoist-pattern[]=*electron*
public-hoist-pattern[]=*node-pty*
